<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  QBX-146. A WRAPPED take column still refuses deletion, and this case pins
  that boundary so it cannot move by accident.

  Step (a) gave take columns a real inverse: SRemoveSampleAction pins the
  clip's object with addRef(), and the inverse re-links the very same object,
  so every take, fade, name, pan, the active index and the comp map come back
  by identity. take_column_delete_undo_restores.qxa gates that, and it is
  12-for-12 reliable.

  IT IS RESTRICTED TO THE DIRECT SHAPE (SLink -> STakeStack), and the reason is
  measured. Re-linking a WRAPPED column (SLink -> SCut -> STakeStack) leaves a
  stale plug in the audio graph: the equivalent case crashed at TEARDOWN, 3
  runs in 12, in

      SApplication::rewireSpeaker
        -> twComponent::setInput( idx=0, newOutput=0 )
          -> oldPlug->getParentLatch().deleteOutput( oldPlug )   SIGSEGV

  while the direct shape passed 12 of 12. Removing the object-to-lane
  disconnect made the wrapped shape WORSE (9 failures in 12), so the disconnect
  is not the cause: an object that was wired, unwired and then re-linked keeps
  graph state a freshly built one does not. SAddSampleAction needs no extra
  rewiring step precisely because it never re-links a previously wired object.

  So a wrapped column keeps step (b)'s refusal. No data loss either way, and no
  intermittent crash. The restore for this shape is tracked separately, with
  that backtrace.

  THIS CASE IS THE BOUNDARY MARKER. When the wrapped restore lands it will
  fail, deliberately, and must be replaced by the round-trip case rather than
  relaxed — the same contract take_delete_refused_not_silent.qxa had before
  step (a) superseded it.

  takestack_wrap_wrapperpan.qxp loads WRAPPED with no environment knob,
  because stakes::foldIsExact refuses to fold a panned wrapper — the refusal a
  user hits in the field.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="take_column_wrapped_delete_refused">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <load-project path="../takestack_wrap_wrapperpan.qxp"/>

    <!-- Really the wrapped shape. If foldIsExact is ever widened this is what
         stops the case silently becoming a second direct-shape test. -->
    <assert-log level="warn" minCount="1"
                contains="take column left WRAPPED: the wrapper is PANNED"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" shape="wrapped" takes="2" placements="1"/>

    <!-- REFUSED, because the pin is restricted to the direct shape. -->
    <remove-sample trackIndex="0" clipIndex="0" timePos="0"
                   expectReject="true"/>
    <assert-log contains="remove-sample: refusing to delete" minCount="1"/>

    <!-- And the column is untouched: still wrapped, still two takes. -->
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" shape="wrapped" takes="2" placements="1"/>

    <!-- Still audible, with the wrapper's hard-left pan intact: channel 1
         silent. A refusal that damaged the clip would be the very bug this
         whole ticket is about. -->
    <render filename="tcwdr.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="2.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="tcwdr.wav" channel="1"
                         minRms="0.0" maxRms="0.0"/>
  </actions>

</SActionScript>
